course: dictionary
lesson: 13507
title: Immobile: not moving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immobile is an adjective. It describes something that is not moving at all, or that cannot move. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The rabbit lay immobile in the long grass, too frightened to move.» The rabbit is frightened and keeping still, so immobile means not moving.
explain: Immobile can also mean that something cannot be moved. «After the fall, Ben's leg was broken, so he was immobile for six weeks.» Ben could not walk because of his injury, so immobile means unable to move.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word. Try «still» in the sentence: «The rabbit lay still in the long grass.» It still makes sense, so immobile means still.
fact: «Immobile» means not moving at all; perfectly still.
fact: «Immobile» can also mean not able to move, for example because of an injury, an illness, or because something is fixed in place.
fact: Plants and barnacles are immobile: they stay in one place all their lives.
fact: Common phrases are stand immobile, lie immobile and completely immobile.
fact: In stories, a frightened character may stand immobile, frozen with fear.
exercise: «The rabbit lay immobile in the long grass.» What does immobile mean here? | Hiding under a bush | Making a loud noise | Running very fast | *Not moving at all
exercise: Which living thing is immobile? | A dog running in the park | A bird flying south | *A barnacle stuck to a rock | A cat chasing a ball
exercise: «After the fall, Ben was immobile for six weeks.» Why was Ben immobile? | Because he was asleep | *Because his leg was broken and he could not move it | Because he was swimming in the sea | Because he was very happy
test: «The statue stood immobile in the square for a hundred years.» What does immobile mean? | Very loud | Shiny and new | *Perfectly still | Able to dance
test: Which word is closest in meaning to immobile? | Noisy | Restless | Speedy | *Still
exam: «Frozen with fear, Maya stood immobile at the top of the stairs.» What does immobile show about Maya? | She was tidying her room | *She could not move, because she was frozen with fear | She was laughing at a joke | She was fast and quick
